# Parameter definitions for thorn Cartoon2DX

BOOLEAN verbose "Print diagnostic information about the cartoon boundary condition"
{
} "no"

# RESTRICTED, not the default PRIVATE: this is a library-wide setting
# meant to be shared by any consumer of the Cartoon2DX math library (e.g.
# CarpetX/Cartoon2DXWaveToyX's own param.ccl does `SHARES: Cartoon2DX;
# USES CCTK_INT order`) -- Cactus's CST rejects USES/EXTENDS on a
# non-RESTRICTED parameter ("attempted to EXTEND or USE non-restricted
# parameter"). Found by an actual build attempt; "GLOBAL:" (tried first)
# isn't a real param.ccl keyword at all -- confirmed by grepping the rest
# of the codebase for it and finding zero other uses, then checking a
# genuinely-working SHARES example (DGWaveToyX/DGCoordinatesX) to find
# the real one.
RESTRICTED:
INT order "Order of the local Lagrange interpolation used to fill cartoon ghost zones (uses order+1 points)"
{
  1:5 :: "linear (2-point) through quintic (6-point), matching the original Cartoon2D thorn's supported range"
} 4

# Original Cartoon2D only stored x>=0 plus a short x<0 hang-over for
# derivative/interpolation stencils; x<0 values come from rotation.
# When yes, xmin should be the axis (0) so the lower-x ghosts are that
# hang-over, and NewRadX::apply_lower_x should be no.
BOOLEAN fill_negative_x "Fill x<0 points by rotation from x>=0 (half-plane cartoon)"
{
} yes

# Deferred, not yet exposed as parameters (see notes.md "Status" for
# rationale):
#   - eno_order / an ENO interpolation option (old Cartoon2D had one;
#     not needed for the vacuum Brill-Lindquist test that motivates this
#     port).
#   - old_excision / new_excision and their associated mask variables
#     (excision is not needed for a vacuum head-on-collision test).
#   - allow_grid_resize (CarpetX grid extents are set directly via
#     CarpetX::ncells_x/y/z etc.; there is no PUGH-style byspacing/byrange
#     grid-resize step to hook).
#   - cartoon_active (fill is invoked from CarpetX apply_boundary_conditions
#     when a face is boundary_t::cartoon, not from a scheduled bin).
